From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Fri, 10 Mar 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: in Tag the monsters of the partner are Tribute material
 and release cost of the team, at n > 2

Owner rule [R-TAG-PARTNER-COST] (ADR-0002): "You may use your partner's cards for costs, Tributes, materials and summon conditions."
The summon Tribute list (field::get_summon_release_list: Tribute Summon, Tribute Set, Duel.GetTributeGroup, GetTributeCount,
CheckTribute, SelectTribute) and the release list of costs and effects (field::get_release_list: Duel.GetReleaseGroup,
CheckReleaseGroup, SelectReleaseGroup and so Duel.CheckReleaseGroupCost, SelectReleaseGroupCost) read the own monster zone and the
zones of the opposing side only. With a partner monster and no own monster the Tribute Summon of a Level 5 monster was not offered
and a release cost could not pay with the partner monster. Now both lists add the monsters of the living partner. They follow the
rules of the own monsters (the same checks; the own half of the releasable mask in the summon list); the hand of the partner is
not added ("your hand" is the own hand only). A partner monster does not free a zone of the summoning duelist, because the zone
logic of the Tribute selection still counts the monsters of the summoner only. Fusion and Ritual material already used the team
(side_cards). Free for all has no partner, so nothing changes there; with two duelists both loops are skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
---
 field.cpp | 41 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 41 insertions(+)

diff --git a/field.cpp b/field.cpp
index f0cee31..a08099f 100644
--- a/field.cpp
+++ b/field.cpp
@@ -2229,6 +2229,23 @@ int32_t field::get_release_list(uint8_t playerid, card_set* release_list, card_s
 			++rcount;
 		}
 	}
+	// More than two duelists (Tag): the monsters of the partner can be released for a cost or an effect like the own ones
+	// ([R-TAG-PARTNER-COST]); the hand of the partner can not ("your hand" is the own hand only). Free for all has no partner. Skipped with two duelists.
+	if(n_duelists > 2) {
+		for(uint8_t q = 0; q < n_duelists; ++q) {
+			if(q == playerid || !is_alive(q) || !same_team(playerid, q))
+				continue;
+			for(auto& pcard : player[q].list_mzone) {
+				if(pcard && pcard != exc && !(exg && exg->has_card(pcard)) && pcard->is_releasable_by_nonsummon(playerid, reason)
+				        && (!fun || pduel->lua->check_matching(pcard, fun, exarg))) {
+					if(release_list)
+						release_list->insert(pcard);
+					pcard->release_param = 1;
+					++rcount;
+				}
+			}
+		}
+	}
 	if(use_hand) {
 		for(auto& pcard : player[playerid].list_hand) {
 			if(pcard && pcard != exc && !(exg && exg->has_card(pcard)) && pcard->is_releasable_by_nonsummon(playerid, reason)
@@ -2342,6 +2359,30 @@ int32_t field::get_summon_release_list(card* target, card_set* release_list, car
 			rcount += pcard->release_param;
 		}
 	}
+	// More than two duelists (Tag): the monsters of the partner are Tribute material of the team ([R-TAG-PARTNER-COST]). They follow the
+	// rules of the own monsters (the same checks, and the own half of the releasable mask), they are no extra release of an opponent.
+	// In free for all nobody has a partner, so the loop finds nothing. With two duelists it is skipped.
+	if(n_duelists > 2) {
+		for(uint8_t q = 0; q < n_duelists; ++q) {
+			if(q == p || !is_alive(q) || !same_team(p, q))
+				continue;
+			for(auto& pcard : player[q].list_mzone) {
+				if(!pcard || !((releasable >> pcard->current.sequence) & 1) || !pcard->is_releasable_by_summon(p, target))
+					continue;
+				if(mg && !mg->has_card(pcard))
+					continue;
+				if(release_list)
+					release_list->insert(pcard);
+				if(pcard->is_affected_by_effect(EFFECT_TRIPLE_TRIBUTE, target))
+					pcard->release_param = 3;
+				else if (pcard->is_affected_by_effect(EFFECT_DOUBLE_TRIBUTE, target))
+					pcard->release_param = 2;
+				else
+					pcard->release_param = 1;
+				rcount += pcard->release_param;
+			}
+		}
+	}
 	uint32_t ex_oneof_max = 0;
 	card_vector oppo_mzone_tmp;
 	for(auto& pcard : side_cards(p, true, &player_info::list_mzone, oppo_mzone_tmp)) {
